  "generated_answer": "## Geometry Learning Objectives \u2014 Class 4 Mathematics\n\n### Unit: Measurement and Estimation GEOMETRY Lines and Angles (C4-U25)\n\nThe geometry content for Class 4 Mathematics is organised under the unit **Measurement and Estimation GEOMETRY Lines and Angles** (code C4-U25). The learning outcomes for this unit are:\n\n- **C4U25-LO01** \u2014 Identify and draw horizontal and vertical lines\n- **C4U25-LO02** \u2014 Identify and draw Perpendicular line and Parallel Lines.\n- **C4U25-LO03** \u2014 Identify and name angles ( equal to, Greater or Less than a right angle).\n- **C4U25-LO04** \u2014 Draw angles ( equal to, Greater or Less than a right angle).\n- **C4U25-LO05** \u2014 Compare angles inside and outside the classroom.\n\nThese outcomes cover the identification and drawing of lines (horizontal, vertical, perpendicular, parallel) and the identification, naming, drawing, and comparison of angles relative to a right angle.",
